{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 (64) code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 (64) code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nconstexpr int BLOCK_SIZE = 1000000;\nconstexpr int MOD1 = 998244353;\nconstexpr int MOD2 = 1000000007;\n\nll n, counter;\nvector<int> buckets[7];\nint bucket_sums[7], answer, total_count;\n\ninline int mod_reduce(ll x) {\n    return static_cast<int>((x % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1);\n}\n\nvoid build_buckets(int depth, ll prefix) {\n    ++counter;\n    buckets[depth].push_back(mod_reduce(counter - prefix));\n    if (depth == 6) return;\n    for (int digit = 0; digit <= 9; ++digit) {\n        build_buckets(depth + 1, prefix * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid query_range(int depth, ll current_value) {\n    if (current_value > n) return;\n    \n    if (depth >= 1) {\n        if (current_value * BLOCK_SIZE > n / 10 && (current_value + 1) * BLOCK_SIZE - 1 <= n) {\n            int multiplier = 1;\n            for (int i = 0; i <= 6; ++i, multiplier *= 10) {\n                int complement = mod_reduce(counter - multiplier * current_value);\n                auto it = lower_bound(buckets[i].begin(), buckets[i].end(), MOD1 - complement);\n                int idx = it - buckets[i].begin();\n                answer = (answer + 1LL * complement * buckets[i].size() % MOD2 + bucket_sums[i] - 1LL * MOD1 * (static_cast<int>(buckets[i].size()) - idx)) % MOD2;\n            }\n            counter += total_count;\n            return;\n        }\n        ++counter;\n        answer = (answer + mod_reduce(counter - current_value)) % MOD2;\n    }\n    \n    for (int digit = (depth == 0); digit <= 9; ++digit) {\n        query_range(depth + 1, current_value * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    build_buckets(0, 0);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= 6; ++i) {\n        sort(buckets[i].begin(), buckets[i].end());\n        bucket_sums[i] = accumulate(buckets[i].begin(), buckets[i].end(), 0LL) % MOD2;\n    }\n    \n    total_count = counter;\n    counter = 0;\n    query_range(0, 0);\n    \n    cout << (answer + MOD2) % MOD2 << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\nfrom functools import reduce\n\ndef main():\n    MOD1 = 998244353\n    MOD2 = 1000000007\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 1000000\n    \n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    n = int(input().strip())\n    \n    counter = 0\n    buckets = [[] for _ in range(7)]\n    \n    def mod_reduce(x):\n        return int((x % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1)\n    \n    def build_buckets(depth, prefix):\n        nonlocal counter\n        counter += 1\n        buckets[depth].append(mod_reduce(counter - prefix))\n        if depth == 6:\n            return\n        for digit in range(10):\n            build_buckets(depth + 1, prefix * 10 + digit)\n    \n    answer = 0\n    \n    def query_range(depth, current_value):\n        nonlocal counter, answer\n        if current_value > n:\n            return\n        \n        if depth >= 1:\n            if current_value * BLOCK_SIZE > n // 10 and (current_value + 1) * BLOCK_SIZE - 1 <= n:\n                multiplier = 1\n                for i in range(7):\n                    complement = mod_reduce(counter - multiplier * current_value)\n                    # Find the first index where buckets[i][idx] >= MOD1 - complement\n                    idx = bisect.bisect_left(buckets[i], MOD1 - complement)\n                    bucket_size = len(buckets[i])\n                    # Calculate the sum contribution\n                    part1 = complement * bucket_size\n                    part2 = bucket_sums[i]\n                    part3 = -MOD1 * (bucket_size - idx)\n                    contribution = (part1 + part2 + part3) % MOD2\n                    answer = (answer + contribution) % MOD2\n                    multiplier *= 10\n                counter += total_count\n                return\n        \n        if depth >= 1:\n            counter += 1\n            answer = (answer + mod_reduce(counter - current_value)) % MOD2\n        \n        start_digit = 0 if depth == 0 else 0\n        for digit in range(start_digit, 10):\n            query_range(depth + 1, current_value * 10 + digit)\n    \n    build_buckets(0, 0)\n    \n    bucket_sums = []\n    for i in range(7):\n        buckets[i].sort()\n        bucket_sums.append(sum(buckets[i]) % MOD2)\n    \n    total_count = counter\n    counter = 0\n    query_range(0, 0)\n    \n    print((answer + MOD2) % MOD2)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013958434283267707, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.034117668867111206, -0.20207975804805756, -5.2569914259947836e-05, -0.349832683801651, -0.002067572670057416, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.5231250524520874, -0.0431942455470562, -0.0328526645898819, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.08869839459657669, -0.014238549396395683, -0.7580256462097168, -0.13004794716835022, -4.7205765440594405e-